    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/8/48365.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 21,
    "turn_text": "So we were getting out, and I'm the one that got it down to 2000 soldiers, but we were going to keep Bagram, not because of Afghanistan, but because of China. It's one hour away from where China makes its nuclear weapons, a nice thing to have. Now I predict that China will be taking that over the base. Bagram was massively expensive many years ago, billions and billions of dollars, and they left. They should have never left. And that's not because of Afghanistan. Again, that's because of China. And all of the things that are happening inflation was caused by energy. And now it's caused by many things. Okay. The energy brought it up to a level that nobody can believe. Oh, inflation is going much higher. Energy is going to go much higher. And I predicted all of this stuff. And I've been good at predicting things, I guess, because I'm hearing a lot about that now from a lot of people, even the radical left. This saying Trump has predicted most of this stuff. But the inflation got the inflation was really started by when the energy we had energy down to less than $2 a gallon for gasoline. We had, I mean, I could go, I could really give you a negative. We had it down to almost nothing a barrel for a while. We had to get it up if you remember, because we were going to destroy the oil companies, the energy companies and the oil companies. But we had it down to $25 and $30 a barrel. Now that was so low that they would not have been able to survive. And we got it up to a little bit more than that.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_02",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
