    "turn_text": "She's been very positive about me and lately very critical because, you know, I'm opposed to her. But you know, club for growth is interesting because they threw a lot of money at somebody named Josh Mandel and I was with JD Vance and as soon as I backed and we club was not doing well. They're having a lot of losses and they came and for two years or so we've been very close and we've had an unblemished record. But when I went for JD Vance, they went out and spent millions and millions of dollars in trying to beat JD Vance. I didn't think that was a nice thing. And what happened is they lost and they lost very badly because you know what people don't know JD was in fourth or fifth place and he was down quite a bit and he came up like a rocket ship. We had a rally for him, but the endorsement and you know then we had a rally and it was great. But they came out and they endorsed one of the opponents who was actually in first place at the time. So they were endorsing the first year. And a lot of times they'll say, well, are you just picking frontrunners? I'm not. I have many people that aren't frontrunners as an example. Well, and I think you can speak to Dr. Oz. Dr. Oz was not winning. He was down nine or 10 points. And now he's leading according, I guess Emerson just came out. He's up by five. So we'll see. But he was down by 10. and now uh... look i've known him for a long time you've known him for a long time he's a very good man i think it would be a great senator i think it will also be able to win the election and i'm not sure that the other people i'm pretty sure that the other people will not be able to win",
